2025-11-08 02:46:45,006 | INFO | ai-engine.app | Received scoring request: {'expectedMeaning': 'User wants to know the process to obtain an Emirates ID', 'actualResponse': 'Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identification card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is essential for accessing government services, opening bank accounts, signing contracts, and more. Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before applying for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriates2.  2. Gather Required Documents   Original passport  Valid UAE residence visa (for expatriates)  One passport-sized photo with a white background (required for children under 15)  Additional documents may be required depending on your nationality, age, or special circumstances45.  3. Submit Your Application  You have two main options:  a) Online Application   Visit the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs and Ports Security (ICP) website or use the ICP mobile app to fill out the Emirates ID application form125.  b) Typing Centre   Go to an accredited typing centre. Staff will assist you in completing the application and uploading your documents245.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Fees vary depending on the validity period of your Emirates ID and your residency status. Payment can be made online or at the typing centre2.  5. Biometric Data Collection   After submitting your application, you will receive an appointment (or can schedule one) at an ICP service centre.  You must visit the centre in person to provide your fingerprints and have your photograph taken (first-time applicants only)25.  6. Track Your Application   You can track the status of your Emirates ID application online using your application number via the ICP website or app15.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   Once your application is approved, you will receive an SMS notification.  Collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office, or it may be delivered to your registered address (depending on your selection during the application)25.  You must collect your card within 90 days of notification5.  8. Urgent Service (Optional)   UAE and GCC nationals can use the “Fawri” urgent service to obtain an Emirates ID within 24 hours for an additional fee. Expatriates can use this service only for card replacement, not for new applications1.  Important Notes   Carry your Emirates ID at all times; it is a legal requirement1.  Companies are not allowed to keep your Emirates ID; they may only record its data15.  If your Emirates ID is lost, stolen, or damaged, report it immediately and apply for a replacement15.  References  1: UAE Government: Emirates ID Application Process & Requirements \n2: First Abu Dhabi Bank: Emirates ID Guide for Newcomers \n3: ICP Official Smart Services Guide (PDF) \n4: Amer Centre: Emirates ID Required Documents \n5: Shuraa: Emirates ID Requirements & Application Steps   If you need guidance on a specific situation (e.g., renewal, replacement, or for children), please let me know for a tailored step-by-step process.    Sources  Ask  Explain    ', 'keywords': [], 'benchmark': 0.3}
