2025-11-08 03:04:37,101 | INFO | ai-engine.app | Received scoring request: {'expectedMeaning': 'User wants to know the process to obtain an Emirates ID', 'actualResponse': 'Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identification card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is issued by the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs & Port Security (ICP) and is essential for accessing government services, banking, healthcare, and more123.  Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before you can apply for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriates3.  2. Prepare Required Documents  The documents needed may vary depending on your nationality and age, but generally include:   Original passport  Valid UAE residence visa (for expatriates)  Birth certificate (for children)  Passport-sized photographs  Supporting documents (as required for special categories, e.g., GCC nationals, newborns)3.  3. Submit Your Application  You have two main options:   Online:  Apply through the official ICP website or ICP mobile app.  In Person:  Visit an accredited typing centre, where staff will help you fill out the application form and collect your documents123.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Fees vary depending on the validity period of your visa and the type of application (new, renewal, replacement).  Payment can be made online or at the typing centre3.  5. Biometric Data Collection   After submitting your application, you will be notified (usually via SMS) to visit an ICP service centre.  At the centre, your fingerprints and photograph will be taken for biometric verification13.  6. Application Processing   The ICP will process your application. You can track the status online or through the ICP app13.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   Once approved, you will receive an SMS notification.  You can collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office, or it may be delivered to your registered address3.  8. Special Services   Urgent Service (Fawri):  UAE and GCC nationals can obtain an Emirates ID within 24 hours for an additional fee. Expatriates can use this service only for card replacement, not initial issuance1.  Important Notes   Carry your Emirates ID at all times; it is a legal requirement.  If your Emirates ID is lost, stolen, or damaged, report it immediately and apply for a replacement1.  Update your details with ICP within one month if there are any changes (e.g., address, marital status)1.  References  1: UAE Government Official Portal – Emirates ID Application Process, Requirements, and FAQs \n2: ICP Official Services – New and Replacement Emirates ID \n3: First Abu Dhabi Bank Expat Guide – Emirates ID Steps and Requirements   If you need more details about specific document requirements or have a unique situation (e.g., newborn, GCC national), please let me know!    Sources  Ask  Explain    ', 'keywords': [], 'benchmark': 0.3}
