2025-11-08 03:14:49,828 | INFO | ai-engine.app | Received scoring request: {'expectedMeaning': 'User wants to know the process to obtain an Emirates ID', 'actualResponse': 'Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identification card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is essential for accessing government services, banking, healthcare, and many daily activities in the UAE. Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before applying for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriates1.  2. Prepare Required Documents  The documents needed may vary depending on your nationality, age, and visa status. Generally, you will need:   Original passport  Valid UAE residence visa  Passport-size photograph  Birth certificate (for children)  Other documents as required by the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs & Port Security (ICP)34.  3. Submit the Application  You have two main options:   Online:  Apply through the ICP website or mobile app.  Typing Centre:  Visit an accredited typing centre, where staff will help you fill out the application form123.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Fees vary depending on the validity period of the card and your residency status.  Payment can be made online or at the typing centre2.  5. Provide Biometric Data   First-time applicants must visit an ICP service centre to give fingerprints and have a photograph taken.  You will be notified (usually by SMS) to schedule this appointment after submitting your application23.  6. Track Your Application   You can check the status of your application online using your application number on the ICP website or app3.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   Once your application is approved, you will receive an SMS notification.  Collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office or as specified in your application. You must pick it up within 90 days23.  8. Special Services   Urgent Service (Fawri):  UAE and GCC nationals can obtain an Emirates ID within 24 hours for an additional fee at select ICP Customer Happiness Centres1.  Important Notes   Always carry your Emirates ID with you; it is illegal for others (including employers) to confiscate your card13.  Report any loss, theft, or damage of your Emirates ID immediately to the ICP and apply for a replacement1.  Renew your Emirates ID within 30 days of expiry to avoid fines13.  References  1: UAE Government: Emirates ID Application Process and Requirements \n2: First Abu Dhabi Bank: Emirates ID Guide \n3: Shuraa: Emirates ID Application & Document Checklist \n4: ICP Official Services Portal   If you need more specific guidance (e.g., for children, newborns, or special cases), please let me know your situation, and I can provide tailored instructions.    Sources  Ask  Explain', 'keywords': [], 'benchmark': 0.3}
