2025-11-08 03:15:37,985 | INFO | ai-engine.app | Received scoring request: {'expectedMeaning': 'User wants to know the process to obtain an Emirates ID', 'actualResponse': 'Step-by-Step Guide: How to Get an Emirates ID  The Emirates ID is a mandatory identity card for all UAE citizens and residents. It is issued by the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs & Port Security (ICP) and is essential for accessing government services, banking, healthcare, and many other aspects of daily life in the UAE13.  Below is a clear, step-by-step guide to obtaining your Emirates ID:  1. Ensure You Have a Valid UAE Residence Visa   You must have a valid UAE residence visa before you can apply for an Emirates ID. This is a strict requirement for expatriate residents3.  2. Prepare Required Documents  Typically, you will need:   A valid passport  A valid UAE residence visa (for expatriates)  Passport-sized photographs  Any additional documents as specified by ICP or your sponsor/employer  3. Submit Your Application  You have two main options:   Online:  Apply through the ICP website or ICP mobile app (availability may depend on your visa type)12.  Typing Centre:  Visit an accredited typing centre, where staff will help you fill out the application and collect your documents3.  4. Pay the Application Fee   Fees vary depending on the validity period of your visa and the type of application (new, renewal, replacement).  Payment can be made online or at the typing centre3.  5. Biometric Data Collection   After submitting your application, you will need to visit an ICP service centre to provide your fingerprints and have your photograph taken.  You can schedule this appointment after your application is submitted3.  6. Application Processing   Once your application is processed, you will receive an SMS notification about the status and next steps3.  7. Collect Your Emirates ID   You can collect your Emirates ID from the designated Emirates Post office, or it may be delivered 